{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"anatomical-arbored-oyster","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Problem\n\nThe scheduled **Test Suite (mirror)** workflow (`.github/workflows/test.yml`) has been red on **every** run for 12+ consecutive scheduled runs (through 2026-08-29). Unlike the tolerated legs, the red is driven by legs that are **NOT** `continue-on-error` and represent **supported** configurations:\n\n- `sweep (macos, full suite)` — macOS + Python 3.13 (installs `uv pip install '.[dev,reviewbot,ui]'`, **non-editable**)\n- `sweep (declared lower-bound resolution)` — Ubuntu + Python 3.11, `--resolution lowest-direct` (**non-editable**)\n\n(The `sweep (windows)` leg is `continue-on-error: true`, and the pre-release interpreter cells — 3.14t/3.15 — are `continue-on-error: ${{ matrix.experimental }}`; those legs' failures, e.g. Windows `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'fcntl'`, are EXPECTED and do not gate. The two legs above are the genuine signal.)\n\n## Decisive evidence (run 33253319934, sha `5fb693345b0c`)\n\n`sweep (macos, full suite)` fails at **collection**:\n```\nERROR collecting tests/unit/test_release_guards.py\nE   FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory:\n    '/Users/runner/work/rebar/rebar/.venv/lib/python3.13/scripts/release_guards.py'\nERROR at setup of test_wheel_from_sdist_bakes_env_commit\nE   FileNotFoundError: ... '/Users/runner/work/rebar/rebar/.venv/lib/python3.13/hatch_build.py'\n```\n`sweep (declared lower-bound resolution)` fails the same way, plus a floor-specific packaging error:\n```\nFileNotFoundError: ... '/home/runner/work/rebar/rebar/.venv/lib/python3.11/scripts/release_guards.py'\nTypeError: Field `project.license-files` must be a table\n  .venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/hatchling/metadata/core.py:725: TypeError\n```\n\n## Root cause\n\n`tests/unit/test_release_guards.py:31` computes the repo root from the installed package:\n```python\nROOT = Path(rebar.__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n_SCRIPT = ROOT / \"scripts\" / \"release_guards.py\"\n```\nUnder an **editable** install (the primary Gerrit Verified Gate / `test.yml` critical path uses `uv sync`/editable), `rebar.__file__` is `src/rebar/__init__.py`, so `parents[2]` is the repo root and `scripts/release_guards.py` exists.\n\nUnder the sweep's **non-editable** install (`uv pip install '.'`), `rebar.__file__` is `<venv>/lib/pythonX/site-packages/rebar/__init__.py`, so `parents[2]` resolves to `<venv>/lib/pythonX/` and `_SCRIPT` becomes `<venv>/lib/pythonX/scripts/release_guards.py` — which is not packaged, hence `FileNotFoundError`. The same editable-layout coupling breaks the packaging tests that reach for the repo-root `hatch_build.py`. These tests are only exercised in the breadth sweep (the critical path runs a `platform_compat` subset), so the defect is invisible on the merge gate.\n\nThe lower-bound `TypeError: Field project.license-files must be a table` is a second, distinct floor issue: the declared minimum `hatchling` predates the current `[project].license-files` string/array form in `pyproject.toml`, so the wheel/sdist build fixtures cannot build at the floor.\n\n## Impact\n\nThe scheduled breadth sweep is chronically red, so it can no longer surface a NEW macOS-only or lower-bound regression — its signal is buried. Per test.yml a red sweep \"gates no merge,\" but these are real test-portability defects on supported platforms that should be green.\n\n## The fix (candidates)\n\n- Make the release/packaging tests locate the repo root independently of the install layout (e.g. skip when `scripts/release_guards.py` / `hatch_build.py` are absent because rebar is installed non-editable, or resolve ROOT via a repo marker rather than `Path(rebar.__file__).parents[2]`), so they self-skip or pass under a non-editable install.\n- Raise the declared `hatchling` floor to a version that accepts the current `[project].license-files` form (or adjust the license-files declaration to satisfy the floor), so the lower-bound resolution can build the wheel/sdist.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `sweep (macos, full suite)` collects and runs `tests/unit/test_release_guards.py` and the sdist/wheel packaging tests without `FileNotFoundError` under a non-editable install.\n- [ ] `sweep (declared lower-bound resolution)` no longer raises `TypeError: Field project.license-files must be a table` at the declared floor.\n- [ ] A `Test Suite (mirror)` scheduled run is green on the non-`continue-on-error` legs (Windows + experimental interpreter legs may remain tolerated).\n\n## Evidence\n- Failing run: https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/33253319934 (sha `5fb693345b0c`)\n- Earlier same failure: https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/33239351184\n- Chronic: `Test Suite (mirror)` has been `failure` on every scheduled run back to at least 2026-08-27.\n- Sweep install steps: `.github/workflows/test.yml` `sweep-macos-full` (`uv pip install '.[dev,reviewbot,ui]'`) and `sweep-lower-bounds` (`uv pip install --resolution lowest-direct '.[dev,agents]'`).","id":"e3e0-2e7c-b280-4b4a","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["ci","test-portability","packaging"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Test Suite (mirror) sweep red on supported legs: release-packaging tests assume an editable/repo-relative layout and fail under the sweep's non-editable install"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788023949772264436,"uuid":"f260b5ea-4256-48ce-9b20-ae37b3832646"}